// Audit 2026-10-03 finding 5: reading a `Scriptor` capability field.
//
// `Scriptor` is `structura Scriptor { a: ambitus, descriptor: i32 }`, but its
// fields are the PRELUDE's, not a program's: the blob reads them by constant
// and a source program has no business with either. The checker used to
// answer `ambitus` for `s.a` and `i32` for `s.descriptor` -- so this program
// TYPE-CHECKED -- and the lowering, which has no case for a prelude field
// (a prelude member carries `Member.d` == 0), died on an `rassert`: `exsc`
// exited 132, SIGILL, on a well-formed program, on both backends. It is not
// an escape (`a` is an `ambitus` the program already holds) and it is not
// forgivable either: a compiler does not trap on input.
//
// The fix is the checker's: `s.a` is `EXS-E0305`, exactly as it is for the
// three ADR 0017 roots (R3). THIS DIRECTORY IS THE END-TO-END HALF --
// `exsc-exit=1` is a diagnostic's exit status, and 132 is the trap. The CODE
// is pinned one layer down, in tests/unit/chk_directorium.asm rows 27-30,
// which also cover a write, an address, a call result and a nested struct.
// The differential phase holds `--emitte c` to the same status.

publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    firma s = Scriptor.ad_exitum(a);
    firma x = s.a;
    redde 0;
}
